  "scope": "The everyday item handlers listed in `unchanged` compiled unchanged on JDK 11 with Kotlin 1.8.20 and the published ConstLib 1.4.28 (Items, Sounds, Scenery, Animations, NPCs and Components values checked against the suffixes of the names used), together with the tables they read and the unchanged OptionHandler, Plugin, Pulse, IntType, core.api.Container, Script, DialogueConst, EquipmentSlot, ApiExtensions, Globals, LoginListener, PersistPlayer, RandomFunction, ChanceItem, WeightedChanceItem and DropFrequency. Original text inserted into adapters at generation time: the Skills ids and SKILL_NAME, StringUtils.isPlusN, NPCDropTables.DROP_RATES and the ContentAPI functions visualize, animate, runTask, getUsedOption, sendChat and getItemFromEquipment. Everything else is a recording adapter answering from the case: the InteractionListeners and InterfaceListeners registries and item definition handler maps (registration is recorded in order), every other ContentAPI function, the player members (attributes with the GameAttributes \"/save:\" rule, locks, animator, pulse manager, packet dispatch, interface manager, dialogue interpreter, inventory, equipment and bank, appearance, diaries, quest repository, skull manager, skills), the world pulser, GroundItemManager, the item definitions table (a HashMap filled in the case order) and the node fields. Each case runs in a class loader of its own and seeds RandomFunction.RANDOM, the generator of Collections.shuffle and the thread's ThreadLocalRandom (Kotlin's Random.Default); the raw state of each is recorded after every operation. Calls made while a class initialises are not recorded.",
